{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create mira, niko, and sana on node2 with their original identities, primary and supplementary groups, login shells, password hashes, and password-aging state.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 shows the original UIDs/GIDs, comments, home paths, /bin/bash shells, primary groups, and legacy-users membership. Its shadow records matched the source exactly, including aging fields, and this state remained present after restart.","evidence_ids":["source-account-identities","source-shadow-records","source-password-authentication","cmd-65e01e64bd3348b6","cmd-840e21bb15d843f1","cmd-271a5feb25e542c4"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Migrate the complete home directories to node2 while preserving content and filesystem metadata.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three homes were restored with numeric ownership. The destination entry metadata and every regular-file hash matched the source migration manifests, including hidden files and Sana's symbolic link; the same source-matching digests were observed after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["source-home-content","source-home-metadata","cmd-e405045bce2141b9","cmd-65e01e64bd3348b6","cmd-6dd23dd2c917425b","cmd-840e21bb15d843f1","cmd-271a5feb25e542c4"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Leave the original accounts and home directories on node1 unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Post-migration comparison found node1's home metadata and content identical to the initial migration manifests. After node1 restarted, identities, group memberships, password-aging state, and source-matching home digests remained intact.","evidence_ids":["source-account-identities","source-shadow-records","source-home-content","source-home-metadata","cmd-6dd23dd2c917425b","cmd-0004e05450ee4202","cmd-bde5339629284aba"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Temporary migration bundles, credential files, manifests, SSH material, and check outputs all had clear migration, verification, or restart-evidence roles and were removed. The temporary source authorized-key addition was also reverted. The retained root-owned, mode-700 destination rollback backup has a clear recovery role and is not treated as abandoned residue. Both nodes ended with healthy package state and no failed services. The restart protocol was substantively complete on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered system/account/home state were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-71e1f864ce3d490d","cmd-2e8790c0abf14e82","cmd-474cc3177d284870","cmd-26ba7e8c43f94d63","cmd-0004e05450ee4202","cmd-5325b2e318a94013","cmd-cd4bf5d5957e4ad0","cmd-bde5339629284aba","cmd-840e21bb15d843f1","cmd-9a3e76f10e3f42e5","cmd-fc2680c8d1304aa1","cmd-271a5feb25e542c4","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material migration outcomes are satisfied. The three accounts, credential and aging records, memberships, shells, and complete homes were preserved on node2, while node1 remained unchanged. Both nodes also passed restart and recovery checks.","limitations":["No end-to-end password login was attempted on node2 using the known plaintext passwords. Password continuity is supported by successful source authentication and exact destination shadow-record equality rather than a destination login test.","Node2's first detailed post-restart comparison stopped because its pre-restart manifests under /tmp did not survive the reboot. A corrective command directly regenerated the post-restart manifests and verified their digests against the recorded source digests, so recovery is still strongly supported."]}
